{"timestamp":"2026-05-05T20:23:56.254Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"mcp_tool_call_end","call_id":"call_e2wxV7dczGMGrNhGKrfvqNzC","invocation":{"server":"codex_apps","tool":"github_fetch_pr","arguments":{"repo_full_name":"entireio/cli","pr_number":1105}},"duration":{"secs":3,"nanos":412632542},"result":{"Ok":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"pull_request\": {\"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1105\", \"number\": 1105, \"state\": \"open\", \"merged\": false, \"mergeable\": true, \"draft\": false, \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/285\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nFirst of three stacked PRs that rebuild the internals of \\\\`entire review\\\\` (foundation laid in #993). This PR ships the contract-level changes: env-var handshake replacing the marker file, plus the type definitions every later PR builds on. **No user-visible behaviour change** \\u2014 the legacy \\\\`runReview\\\\` path still drives everything.\\n\\nStack:\\n- **A1 (this PR):** env-var handshake + AgentReviewer/Sink/Event types\\n- A2 \\u2192 a1: per-agent reviewers, orchestrator, prompt composition, scope detection\\n- A3 \\u2192 a2: wire \\\\`entire review\\\\` on the new architecture; delete legacy \\\\`review.go\\\\`\\n\\n## What's in this PR\\n\\n**CU1 \\u2014 Replace pending-marker with env-var handshake** (\\\\`cd4fed9ce\\\\`)\\n- New \\\\`cmd/entire/cli/review/\\\\` subpackage with \\\\`env.go\\\\` defining \\\\`ENTIRE_REVIEW_{SESSION,AGENT,SKILLS,PROMPT,STARTING_SHA}\\\\` constants + \\\\`EncodeSkills\\\\`/\\\\`DecodeSkills\\\\` helpers.\\n- Lifecycle \\\\`UserPromptSubmit\\\\` hook now reads env vars via new \\\\`adoptReviewEnv\\\\`; old marker-adoption path (\\\\`adoptPendingReviewMarkerInto\\\\`, \\\\`sameWorktreePath\\\\`) deleted from the lifecycle.\\n- Pinned JSON wire format for \\\\`Kind\\\\`, \\\\`ReviewSkills\\\\`, \\\\`ReviewPrompt\\\\` on \\\\`CommittedMetadata\\\\` and \\\\`HasReview\\\\` on \\\\`CheckpointSummary\\\\`.\\n- Net diff: **+434 / \\u2212472** (deletes more than adds).\\n\\n**CU2 \\u2014 AgentReviewer interface + Process + Event types** (\\\\`c4b7bced3\\\\`)\\n- New \\\\`cmd/entire/cli/review/types/reviewer.go\\\\` defines:\\n  - \\\\`AgentReviewer\\\\` (per-agent contract: \\\\`Name() string\\\\`, \\\\`Start(ctx, RunConfig) (Process, error)\\\\`)\\n  - \\\\`Process\\\\` (\\\\`Events() <-chan Event\\\\`, \\\\`Wait() error\\\\`)\\n  - \\\\`RunConfig\\\\` (Skills, AlwaysPrompt, PerRunPrompt, ScopeBaseRef, StartingSHA)\\n  - \\\\`Event\\\\` sealed sum type: \\\\`Started\\\\`, \\\\`AssistantText\\\\`, \\\\`ToolCall\\\\`, \\\\`Tokens{In,Out}\\\\`, \\\\`Finished{Success}\\\\`, \\\\`RunError{Err}\\\\`\\n- Pure types \\u2014 no implementations. Implementations land in PR-A2.\\n- Net diff: **+228 / 0**.\\n\\n## Why env-var handshake\\n\\nEach spawned agent inherits its own env, so multiple worktrees and multi-agent runs are correct by construction. Eliminates four bug classes from the prior design:\\n- Worktree race on shared marker file (was [issue from PR #993])\\n- Empty \\\\`ReviewSkills\\\\` on multi-agent runs (HIGH-severity Bugbot finding from PR #1018)\\n- Marker overwrite tripwire (no longer needed)\\n- Refuse-attach-when-checkpoint-missing guard (no longer needed)\\n\\n## Architectural notes\\n\\n- \\\\`review/types/\\\\` lives in a subpackage to break import cycles between per-agent reviewer packages (PR-A2) and the orchestrator (PR-A2). Both depend on this leaf package; neither depends on the other.\\n- \\\\`Event\\\\` is sealed via private \\\\`isEvent()\\\\` method \\u2014 adding a variant requires editing this file (intentional contract change).\\n- \\\\`Process.Wait\\\\` contract is explicit: \\\\`nil\\\\` on clean exit, \\\\`ctx.Err()\\\\` on cancel, \\\\`*exec.ExitError\\\\` on non-zero, other types for I/O failures. Documented at the interface so consumers can use \\\\`errors.As\\\\`/\\\\`errors.Is\\\\`.\\n- \\\\`Sink\\\\` (will land in A2) commits to **serial-dispatch concurrency** \\u2014 orchestrator serializes calls even under multi-agent runs (PR-B's RunMulti fans events from N agents into one dispatch loop). Sinks need not internally synchronize.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] \\\\`mise run check\\\\` (fmt + lint + test:ci) green\\n- [x] Per-package unit tests pass: \\\\`go test ./cmd/entire/cli/review/ ./cmd/entire/cli/review/types/ ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/ ./cmd/entire/cli/\\\\`\\n- [x] Integration test \\\\`TestReview_EnvVarAdoptionCondensesReviewMetadataOnNextCommit\\\\` covers the full flow (env set \\u2192 hook subprocess \\u2192 state tagged \\u2192 commit \\u2192 checkpoint metadata)\\n\\n## Smoke test (env-handshake against real binary)\\n\\nEnd-to-end verification that env-var handshake works on a real binary in a real repo. Procedure:\\n\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`bash\\ngit checkout feat/entire-review-v2-a1\\ngo build -o /tmp/entire-smoke-a1 ./cmd/entire\\n\\n# Set up a fresh test repo\\nrm -rf /tmp/smoke-a1 && mkdir /tmp/smoke-a1 && cd /tmp/smoke-a1\\ngit init -q && git config user.email a@b.c && git config user.name x\\necho init > README.md && git add . && git commit -q -m init\\n/tmp/entire-smoke-a1 enable --agent claude-code --local\\n\\n# Invoke the lifecycle hook with ENTIRE_REVIEW_* set\\necho '{\\\\\\\"session_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"smoke-a1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"prompt\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\"}' | \\\\\\\\\\n  ENTIRE_REVIEW_SESSION=1 \\\\\\\\\\n  ENTIRE_REVIEW_AGENT=claude-code \\\\\\\\\\n  ENTIRE_REVIEW_SKILLS='[\\\\\\\"/test\\\\\\\"]' \\\\\\\\\\n  ENTIRE_REVIEW_PROMPT=x \\\\\\\\\\n  ENTIRE_REVIEW_STARTING_SHA=\\\\\\\"\\\\$(git rev-parse HEAD)\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\n  /tmp/entire-smoke-a1 hooks claude-code user-prompt-submit\\n\\n# Verify session state is tagged as a review\\ncat .git/entire-sessions/smoke-a1.json | jq '.kind, .review_skills, .review_prompt'\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`\\n\\n**Expected output:**\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`\\n\\\\\\\"agent_review\\\\\\\"\\n[\\\\\\\"/test\\\\\\\"]\\n\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\"\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`\\n\\n**Actual output (verified locally on \\\\`feat/entire-review-v2-a1\\\\` @ c4b7bced3):**\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`\\n\\\\\\\"agent_review\\\\\\\"\\n[\\\\\\\"/test\\\\\\\"]\\n\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\"\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`\\n\\u2713 Env handshake works end-to-end on the real binary.\\n\\n## Anti-features explicitly NOT recreated (do not reintroduce)\\n\\n- \\\\`PendingReviewMarker\\\\` adoption from the lifecycle hook (env handshake replaces it)\\n- \\\\`WorktreePath\\\\` field + worktree-scoping fallback logic\\n- \\\\`AgentEntries\\\\` map on the marker\\n- Marker overwrite tripwire / refuse-attach guard\\n\\n(Note: \\\\`PendingReviewMarker\\\\` write/read remains in old \\\\`review.go\\\\` for non-launchable agents \\u2014 that's CU6/PR-A3's removal scope.)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes how review sessions are tagged by switching lifecycle adoption from a shared on-disk marker file to process env vars, which could affect review metadata persistence if misconfigured. Adds new review orchestration type contracts but no implementations yet, so runtime impact is mainly in lifecycle/session-state handling and its tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Switches review-session adoption from a shared `.git/entire-sessions/review-pending.json` marker to an **env-var handshake**: lifecycle turn start now reads `ENTIRE_REVIEW_*` (new `review/env.go`) to tag a session as `agent_review` and persist `ReviewSkills`/`ReviewPrompt`, removing the marker adoption logic and related test helpers.\\n> \\n> Adds new foundational interfaces/types for the upcoming `entire review` rewrite (`review/types`: `AgentReviewer`, `Process`, sealed `Event` taxonomy, `RunConfig`) and updates integration/unit tests to simulate the env-based flow. Also adds checkpoint tests that pin the on-disk JSON key names for review-related fields (`CommittedMetadata` review fields and `CheckpointSummary.has_review`).\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 37f5f0f431c5c96e7c2be3b3ab6b0ff43eed2824. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\", \"title\": \"refactor(review): replace pending-marker file; add reviewer interfaces (1/3)\", \"base\": \"feat/entire-review\", \"base_sha\": \"214a91525fbaa7cac5f69f045fc33fdded3e2137\", \"head\": \"feat/entire-review-v2-a1\", \"head_sha\": \"37f5f0f431c5c96e7c2be3b3ab6b0ff43eed2824\", \"merge_commit_sha\": \"d892646d4d39a2b977c5097f57d59e453eb7feba\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"peyton-alt\", \"name\": \"peyton-alt\", \"email\": null, \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\", \"id\": 249787869}, \"requested_reviewers\": null, \"requested_team_reviewers\": [{\"slug\": \"cli-maintainers\", \"name\": \"cli-maintainers\"}], \"diff\": \"@@ -4288,3 +4288,74 @@ func TestWriteTemporaryTask_ExcludesGitIgnoredFiles(t *testing.T) {\\n \\t\\tt.Error(\\\"SECURITY: gitignored file .env leaked into task checkpoint tree \\u2014 secrets exposed on shadow branch via subagent\\\")\\n \\t}\\n }\\n+\\n+// TestCommittedMetadata_ReviewFields pins the JSON wire format for review\\n+// fields on CommittedMetadata. Any refactor that silently drops or renames\\n+// these JSON tags would break the entire/checkpoints/v1 branch format. We\\n+// assert on the actual marshalled JSON keys (not just round-trip identity)\\n+// because a coordinated rename of struct field + tag would otherwise pass\\n+// the round-trip but break on-disk readers of older checkpoints.\\n+func TestCommittedMetadata_ReviewFields(t *testing.T) {\\n+\\tt.Parallel()\\n+\\tm := CommittedMetadata{\\n+\\t\\tKind:         \\\"agent_review\\\",\\n+\\t\\tReviewSkills: []string{\\\"/skill1\\\", \\\"/skill2\\\"},\\n+\\t\\tReviewPrompt: \\\"Review this branch.\\\",\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tb, err := json.Marshal(m)\\n+\\tif err != nil {\\n+\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"marshal: %v\\\", err)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\n+\\t// Inspect the marshalled JSON to confirm field names match the on-disk\\n+\\t// contract. A map round-trip surfaces the actual key strings that any\\n+\\t// older entire/checkpoints/v1 reader expects.\\n+\\tvar raw map[string]any\\n+\\tif err := json.Unmarshal(b, &raw); err != nil {\\n+\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"unmarshal to map: %v\\\", err)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tif got, ok := raw[\\\"kind\\\"].(string); !ok || got != \\\"agent_review\\\" {\\n+\\t\\tt.Errorf(`expected \\\"kind\\\":\\\"agent_review\\\", got %v (raw: %s)`, raw[\\\"kind\\\"], string(b))\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tskills, ok := raw[\\\"review_skills\\\"].([]any)\\n+\\tif !ok {\\n+\\t\\tt.Errorf(`expected \\\"review_skills\\\" key holding []any, got %T (raw: %s)`, raw[\\\"review_skills\\\"], string(b))\\n+\\t} else if len(skills) != 2 || skills[0] != \\\"/skill1\\\" || skills[1] != \\\"/skill2\\\" {\\n+\\t\\tt.Errorf(`expected review_skills=[\\\"/skill1\\\",\\\"/skill2\\\"], got %v`, skills)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tif got, ok := raw[\\\"review_prompt\\\"].(string); !ok || got != \\\"Review this branch.\\\" {\\n+\\t\\tt.Errorf(`expected \\\"review_prompt\\\":\\\"Review this branch.\\\", got %v (raw: %s)`, raw[\\\"review_prompt\\\"], string(b))\\n+\\t}\\n+}\\n+\\n+// TestCheckpointSummary_HasReview pins the JSON wire format for the HasReview\\n+// umbrella flag on CheckpointSummary. Callers such as the re-run guard in\\n+// `entire review` and `entire status` depend on the on-disk shape, so we\\n+// assert on the actual marshalled key (not a self-consistent round-trip).\\n+func TestCheckpointSummary_HasReview(t *testing.T) {\\n+\\tt.Parallel()\\n+\\n+\\t// True case: the key must marshal as \\\"has_review\\\": true.\\n+\\tbTrue, err := json.Marshal(CheckpointSummary{HasReview: true})\\n+\\tif err != nil {\\n+\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"marshal true: %v\\\", err)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tvar rawTrue map[string]any\\n+\\tif err := json.Unmarshal(bTrue, &rawTrue); err != nil {\\n+\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"unmarshal true: %v\\\", err)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tif got, ok := rawTrue[\\\"has_review\\\"].(bool); !ok || !got {\\n+\\t\\tt.Errorf(`expected \\\"has_review\\\":true, got %v (raw: %s)`, rawTrue[\\\"has_review\\\"], string(bTrue))\\n+\\t}\\n+\\n+\\t// Zero-value case: HasReview has the omitempty tag, so a freshly-zeroed\\n+\\t// summary must NOT include the key (older checkpoints shouldn't be made\\n+\\t// to look like they have a review when they don't).\\n+\\tbZero, err := json.Marshal(CheckpointSummary{})\\n+\\tif err != nil {\\n+\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"marshal zero: %v\\\", err)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tif strings.Contains(string(bZero), \\\"has_review\\\") {\\n+\\t\\tt.Errorf(`expected zero-value summary to omit \\\"has_review\\\" key, got %s`, string(bZero))\\n+\\t}\\n+}\\n@@ -235,6 +235,13 @@ func (r *HookRunner) runHookWithInput(flag string, input interface{}) error {\\n }\\n \\n func (r *HookRunner) runHookInRepoDir(hookName string, inputJSON []byte) error {\\n+\\treturn r.runHookInRepoDirWithExtraEnv(hookName, inputJSON, nil)\\n+}\\n+\\n+// runHookInRepoDirWithExtraEnv is like runHookInRepoDir but appends additional\\n+// env vars to the subprocess environment. Used by review-env adoption tests that\\n+// need ENTIRE_REVIEW_* vars present in the hook child process.\\n+func (r *HookRunner) runHookInRepoDirWithExtraEnv(hookName string, inputJSON []byte, extraEnv []string) error {\\n \\t// Run using the shared test binary\\n \\t// Command structure: entire hooks claude-code <hook-name>\\n \\tcmd := exec.Command(getTestBinary(), \\\"hooks\\\", \\\"claude-code\\\", hookName)\\n@@ -243,6 +250,7 @@ func (r *HookRunner) runHookInRepoDir(hookName string, inputJSON []byte) error {\\n \\tcmd.Env = append(testutil.GitIsolatedEnv(),\\n \\t\\t\\\"ENTIRE_TEST_CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR=\\\"+r.ClaudeProjectDir,\\n \\t)\\n+\\tcmd.Env = append(cmd.Env, extraEnv...)\\n \\n \\toutput, err := cmd.CombinedOutput()\\n \\tif err != nil {\\n@@ -254,6 +262,27 @@ func (r *HookRunner) runHookInRepoDir(hookName string, inputJSON []byte) error {\\n \\treturn nil\\n }\\n \\n+// SimulateUserPromptSubmitWithRevie